# DIAGNOSTICS

Without the EGL library it prints `Error loading EGL library` and exits with 1.
A failure of EGL or GL is glmark2's message, `Error:` and what failed.

# BUGS

There is no full screen: `--fullscreen` prints `Error: VectraOS has no full screen window: give --size` and exits.
Closing the window doesn't end a run: EGL gives the program no window events.
`--results-file` and `--validate`'s screenshots are written through the file library, so only to a namespace with somewhere to write.
Each scene's idle and system time, which glmark2 reads from `/proc/uptime` and getrusage(2), are not shown: there is no `/proc/uptime`, and all of the CPU time is user time.
